      "Scheduled routine, branch claude/upbeat-dijkstra-5aqb5x. HEAD started at 16d550be (PR #936, outreach-followup-cron-automation, merged this session's own prior PR). A dispatched research agent was told to find the next high-leverage, non-repeated business/code gap, explicitly warned off a fourth cron-automation route unless well-evidenced (three shipped this same day already covers the obvious instances of that shape). It surfaced and I independently re-verified three candidates before picking one: (1) client-facing analytics/reporting for paying customers — ruled out as too large a redesign, since no client-auth model exists anywhere in the app (only operator auth via requireOperatorAuth); (2) a discount/referral mechanism — ruled out as already fully built (POST /api/stripe/checkout already sets allow_promotion_codes on every Session, with total_details.amount_discount reconciliation in the webhook); (3) an annual billing option for Growth/Complete bundle checkouts, alongside the existing monthly-only recurring price — genuinely unbuilt, grep-confirmed (no 'annual' or 'year' interval anywhere in src/lib/pricing or the checkout/webhook routes), and a real, common SaaS revenue lever (lower payment-processing overhead, better cash flow, lower churn risk) with no client-auth or legal-review prerequisite.",
